/*
 * pg_multirangetypes_io.c: vendored PostgreSQL C oracle for the
 * multirangetypes_diff differential fuzz target (100%-coverage campaign;
 * crate crates/backend/utils/adt/multirangetypes).
 *
 * GENERATED by the lane assembler (scratchpad mrsrc/assemble_mr.py) from
 * VERBATIM upstream extracts — regenerate rather than hand-editing bodies.
 *
 * Provenance (ALL bodies verbatim, upstream sha
 * 62d6c7d3df6287f1bd83199c1a746e50d31571a0 = PostgreSQL 18.3 Stamp-18.3):
 *   - src/backend/utils/adt/multirangetypes.c: the full non-aggregate
 *     surface — multirange_in/out/recv/send + get_multirange_io_data,
 *     the NORMALIZATION KERNEL (multirange_canonicalize, qsort_arg over
 *     range_compare, then the adjacent/before/union merge walk),
 *     multirange_size_estimate/write_multirange_data/make_multirange,
 *     multirange_deserialize/get_range/get_bounds/get_bounds_offset/
 *     get_union_range/make_empty_multirange, the bsearch helpers
 *     (range_bounds_overlaps, range_bounds_contains,
 *     multirange_bsearch_match + the three comparison callbacks),
 *     constructors 0/1/2, accessors (lower/upper/empty/lower_inc/upper_inc/
 *     lower_inf/upper_inf), the complete operator family in all
 *     range x multirange / multirange x range / multirange x multirange
 *     forms (eq/ne/lt/le/ge/gt/cmp, overlaps, contains, contained_by,
 *     adjacent, before, after, overleft, overright, contains_elem,
 *     elem_contained_by, each fmgr wrapper + its _internal), set ops
 *     (union/minus/intersect + the two _internal merge walks),
 *     range_merge_from_multirange, hash_multirange(+extended).
 *     CARVED OUT (lane carve, recorded as exception rows — their pure
 *     delegates ARE reached through the non-aggregate entries):
 *     range_agg_transfn, range_agg_finalfn, multirange_agg_transfn,
 *     multirange_intersect_agg_transfn (aggregate transition state),
 *     multirange_unnest (SRF machinery).
 *   - src/backend/utils/adt/rangetypes.c: range_compare (the qsort_arg
 *     callback multirange_canonicalize sorts with; NOT in the range
 *     oracle's extract list, so this is its only definition).
 *   - src/backend/utils/adt/arrayfuncs.c: deconstruct_array, and
 *     src/backend/utils/adt/arrayutils.c: ArrayGetNItems(+Safe) — the
 *     multirange_constructor2 variadic-array path.
 *   - src/port/qsort_arg.c over src/include/lib/sort_template.h (both
 *     verbatim): C's exact sort, so within-tie ordering is C's own.
 *   - src/include/utils/multirangetypes.h: MultirangeType + its accessor
 *     macros; src/include/utils/array.h: ArrayType + the ARR_* macros.
 *
 * ============ STRUCTURE: ONE TRANSLATION UNIT WITH THE RANGE ORACLE ============
 * This file #includes csrc/pg_rangetypes_io.c. multirangetypes.c calls
 * fourteen rangetypes.c functions (make_range, make_empty_range,
 * range_deserialize, range_cmp_bounds, bounds_adjacent, and the
 * contains/overlaps/before/adjacent/overleft/minus/union/intersect/split
 * _internal family) plus the shared typcache mock, palloc arena,
 * ereport/longjmp shim and StringInfo/pqformat shims — all of which are
 * `static` in that file (its shim 8). Re-vendoring them here would create a
 * second, silently divergent copy; extern-promoting ~40 statics would be a
 * large edit to a file another lane owns concurrently. Including it costs one
 * line, keeps the range oracle byte-identical, and guarantees both targets
 * diff against the SAME vendored range code.
 *   => build.rs compiles ONLY this file. pg_rangetypes_io.c must NOT also be
 *      listed there, or every non-static pg_diff_* entry is defined twice.
 *   => The ONE edit made to pg_rangetypes_io.c is the additive
 *      `TypeCacheEntry.rngtype` field (marked in that file): the real
 *      typcache entry carries it and the verbatim multirange bodies read it.
 *      Re-apply it if that file is regenerated.
 *
 * SHIMS (plumbing only, never logic) — the range oracle's shims 1-8 apply
 * unchanged; this file adds:
 *   A. MULTIRANGE TYPCACHE SEAM (extends the sanctioned mock, mirrored
 *      EXACTLY by the Rust driver): pg_mr_lookup / multirange_get_typcache
 *      return static TypeCacheEntry values for the pinned instantiations
 *        int4multirange 4451 (align 'i')  rngtype = int4range 3904
 *        nummultirange  4532 (align 'i')  rngtype = numrange  3906
 *        int8multirange 4536 (align 'd')  rngtype = int8range 3926
 *      (pg_type.dat @ the pinned sha; typlen -1, byval false, storage 'x',
 *      typtype 'm'). The fn_extra memo is elided exactly as
 *      range_get_typcache's is — a pure cache with no behavioral surface.
 *   B. get_multirange_io_data's element I/O lookup -> pg_mr_get_range_io,
 *      dispatching the range type's OWN range_in/out/recv/send (which the
 *      range oracle defines), mirroring the shipped
 *      cached_multirange_io_data path.
 *   C. Two errcode CLASSES the range oracle's table lacks (the Rust driver
 *      mirrors the numbers): 12 = 21000 ERRCODE_CARDINALITY_VIOLATION,
 *      13 = 22004 ERRCODE_NULL_VALUE_NOT_ALLOWED.
 *   D. deconstruct_array's Assert(ARR_ELEMTYPE == elmtype) is the no-op
 *      Assert of the shared prelude, as in a real NDEBUG build.
 */

#include "pg_rangetypes_io.c"
